<hr/>

<h2>1. System Overview & Architecture</h2>
<p>The <strong>JSR Retails & Sales Management System</strong> is an enterprise retail Point of Sale (POS), Inventory Control, Multi-Party Ledger Accounting, and Day-End Cash Reconciliation platform engineered specifically for high-speed retail operations in India.</p>

<h3>Key Architectural Principles:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Reactive Single-Page Architecture:</strong> Built on Next.js 14 App Router and React 18, providing sub-millisecond tab switching without page reload latency.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloud-Native Database:</strong> Powered by Supabase PostgreSQL with real-time WebSocket broadcast sync (<code>sync_settings</code>, party ledgers).</li>
  <li><strong>Dual Thermal Printing Engine:</strong> Native ESC/POS formatted 58mm and 80mm thermal receipts with store logo, GST tax summary, and Telugu bilingual descriptions.</li>
  <li><strong>Fully Responsive Layout:</strong> Engineered for seamless usability across mobile phones, tablets, POS terminals, and large widescreen desktop monitors.</li>
</ul>

<hr/>

<h2>2. User Roles & Access Control</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Role Name</th>
    <th>Access Level</th>
    <th>Operational Scope</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Admin</strong></td>
    <td>Superuser Access</td>
    <td>Complete access to POS, Invoices, Procurements, Accounting, Lenders, Partner Capitals, Master Settings, 2FA credentials, and system audit logs.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Partner</strong></td>
    <td>Management Access</td>
    <td>Full access to business operations, partner capital drawdowns, financial snapshots, and daily approvals.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Staff / Cashier</strong></td>
    <td>Operational Access</td>
    <td>Dedicated access to POS Billing, Invoice search, basic collections, and daily receipts without access to master profit margins or system secrets.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Customer Portal</strong></td>
    <td>Self-Service</td>
    <td>Customer view restricted to personal invoices, receipts, payment history, outstanding balance, and statement downloads.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Supplier Portal</strong></td>
    <td>Self-Service</td>
    <td>Vendor view restricted to purchase orders, payment receipts, outstanding balances, and supply history.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Dual Portal</strong></td>
    <td>Combined Self-Service</td>
    <td>For parties that act as both customer and supplier (contra accounts), allowing unified balance and ledger access.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>3. Authentication & Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dual-Mode Login Experience:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><em>Staff & Admin Mode:</em> 4-digit PIN authentication with optional 2FA TOTP verification.</li>
      <li><em>Party Portal Mode:</em> Direct mobile phone number lookup with OTP/PIN authorization.</li>
      <li><em>Desktop Split-Screen UI:</em> 75% widescreen visual showcase and 25% clean authorization form.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA TOTP):</strong> Compliant with RFC 6238 time-based tokens. Generates rolling 30-second security codes with emergency administrative override keys.</li>
  <li><strong>Session Persistence & Protection:</strong> Automatic session clearance upon browser closure or logout, with PIN re-entry requested for administrative settings.</li>
</ul>

<hr/>

<h2>4. Core Business Modules & Workflows</h2>

<h3>4.1 POS Billing & Cash Register</h3>
<p>Enables ultra-fast billing with barcode scanning or keyword lookup. Automatically updates inventory stock in real time, computes line item discounts, and offers flexible payment options (Cash, UPI, Split Payment, or Advance Adjusted). Directly prints 58mm/80mm receipts.</p>

<h3>4.2 Invoices & Receipts Management</h3>
<p>Provides complete search and filtering across all generated sales invoices. Equipped with horizontal scrolling to guarantee that mobile devices display invoice details without letter-by-letter vertical wrapping.</p>

<h3>4.3 Purchases & Inventory Management</h3>
<p>Enables recording multi-line purchase orders from suppliers. Automatically tracks individual purchase rates, target sale rates, and remaining batch stocks.</p>

<h3>4.4 Low Stock Alert & 1-Click Reorder Hub</h3>
<p>Real-time visual badge in the header shows items reaching or breaching reorder thresholds. The 1-Click Auto Reorder feature automatically prepares purchase orders using preferred suppliers and predefined quantities.</p>

<h3>4.5 Payments & Collections (Party Ledgers)</h3>
<p>Comprehensive ledger settlement supporting both single-bill targeting and multi-bill FIFO auto-allocation. Correctly updates customer dues, accounts payable, and partner cash/UPI accounts.</p>

<h3>4.6 Customer Credit Limit Control & Admin Override</h3>
<p>Protects business liquidity by enforcing customer credit limits. Alerts cashiers and blocks invoice submission if the new sale exceeds the customer's credit cap, unless authorized via the <em>Admin Override Approved</em> checkbox.</p>

<h3>4.7 Automated WhatsApp Payment Reminders</h3>
<p>Enables sending 1-click WhatsApp payment reminders with store details, amount due, and UPI payment information directly to customers via the Meta WhatsApp Cloud API.</p>

<h3>4.8 Day-End Cash Register Reconciliation (Z-Report)</h3>
<p>Provides strict end-of-day cash reconciliation based on the exact formula:</p>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>Expected Cash</strong> = Opening Cash + Cash Sales + Cash Collections - Cash Expenses - Supplier Cash Paid
</div>
<p>Cashiers enter counts of physical currency notes (₹500, ₹200, ₹100, ₹50, ₹20, ₹10, Coins), and the system detects and records any <strong>Surplus</strong> or <strong>Shortage</strong> with thermal receipt printout.</p>

<h3>4.9 Indian Number Format (en-IN) Comma Separation</h3>
<p>All numeric displays and inputs automatically format values using the Indian numbering system:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>1000</code> &rarr; <strong>1,000</strong></li>
  <li><code>10000</code> &rarr; <strong>10,000</strong></li>
  <li><code>100000</code> &rarr; <strong>1,00,000</strong></li>
  <li><code>1000000</code> &rarr; <strong>10,00,000</strong></li>
  <li><code>2500000.50</code> &rarr; <strong>25,00,000.50</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Integrated <code>IndianNumberInput</code> maintains cursor position smoothly during typing, while <code>cleanNum()</code> preserves 100% calculation and database integrity.</p>

<hr/>

<h2>5. Database Schema & Data Model</h2>
<p>PostgreSQL schema on Supabase with the following primary relational tables:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>customers</code>: Customer master profiles, phone numbers, opening balances, and credit limits.</li>
  <li><code>suppliers</code>: Vendor master profiles, phone numbers, and opening payables.</li>
  <li><code>items</code>: Inventory item catalog, cost rates, sale rates, stock counts, reorder thresholds, and suggested quantities.</li>
  <li><code>procurements</code>: Goods receipts, purchase batches, PO numbers, and vendor disbursement records.</li>
  <li><code>invoices</code>: Sales bills, customer links, totals, upfront payments, balance dues, and itemized JSON records.</li>
  <li><code>collections</code>: Inward payment collections received from customers with partner attribution.</li>
  <li><code>expenses</code>: Daily operating expenditure entries categorized with partner attribution.</li>
  <li><code>receivers</code>: Partner master records tracking individual cash and UPI balance accounts.</li>
  <li><code>borrowers</code>: Business loan sources and outstanding principal balances.</li>
  <li><code>loan_payments</code>: Repayments split by principal and interest.</li>
  <li><code>system_settings</code>: Master configuration document (JSONB) synced across all clients.</li>
  <li><code>z_reports</code>: Daily cash drawer reconciliation logs and denomination counts.</li>
</ul>

